 "notes": [
  "The 'two separate groups' warning is not a real problem, so I kept the graph as it is. The booklet builds two separate models: the red mailbox on page 3 (b1-b6) and the mail van on pages 4-15 (b7-b62). Nothing in the booklet joins them. The mailbox is only shown standing beside the van on page 15. Joining them would add a connection the manual does not show.",
  "Parts list totals 62 pieces and all are listed (b1-b62). The minifigure on page 2 is not in the parts list, so it has no entry.",
  "Booklet pictures are small, so some placements are best guesses. This applies mainly to which door-rail plates go front or rear, which 1x4 and 1x3 pieces go where, the red tiles and plates, and the slope 3037 (put on the hood in step 16).",
  "Pieces that sit under another piece and were added later have rests_on [] and an other_join instead. This covers the mailbox stand under the box and the wheel holders under the base.",
  "The van's 4 tyres and 4 wheels are each pressed together, and the wheel pins into the holders b13 (front) and b14 (rear).",
  "The sticker sheet is one piece. Its stickers go on the 1x4x1 panels (7731 and envelope) and on the roof piece b61."
 ],
